The sample teardown-inputs.ts and its test read. evidence/ is real, cut to one launch; export.json is written by hand and is no run of the private render.

evidence/rows.jsonl is the controller-headless/omp line of a prompt-inputs proof's rows.jsonl, byte for byte, and evidence/composition.json is the same run's composition.json with only that launch left in its two launch tables. The run is the stand-in run base-standin-a12 of 2026-11-26 (rows.jsonl written 11:51:51Z), whose subject and base were both ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25, and whose proof.log ends `--- PASS: TestPromptInputsLive`. Its two parts are that commit's packages/daemon/internal/prompts/roles/controller-root.md and go/controller-headless.md, whose bytes and sha256 the row gives. The command, from a checkout at that commit, with LEGION_OMP_PATH set:

bash scripts/e2e/prompt-inputs.sh --subject <checkout at ecd967b17a4e527009dab56f459e0f4e76c0bd25>

Not captured: export.json. The private render has written no export of the schema prompt-render/2 yet. This one is written in that render's export types (Export, PublicRef, Render, LaunchRow, PartRow, Digest and Control, as its source declares them for prompt-render/1), with the schema prompt-render/2 and the `composed` and `memoryFile` digests that the render's plan adds in that version. Its projects are the neutral ACME and BETA, its private checkout is labelled `main` at a neutral commit, and its public branch is the neutral `sample-branch`. Each launch's parts are the row's two parts under their repository path. roleText and assembled are composed by the render's rule from those two files and a one-line neutral deployment text: "Sample shared deployment text.\n", then "\n", then "Sample deployment text of ACME.\n" (or BETA), under the header "# Deployment instructions (<project>)", and BETA's memory text "Sample memory text of BETA.\n". The real before and after exports are fixture F6, captured from the private render's own runs.
